{
 "rater": "single rater, mechanical check against the written rule; see paper/matcher_validation.md",
 "labelled": "2026-07-30",
 "rules": [
  "A commit is `genuine` if AT LEAST ONE matched key refers to work done in that commit. This mirrors the citation rate being validated, which counts a commit as citing a ticket on >=1 match. Commits carrying both their own ticket and a reference to other work (e.g. `HIVE-13876: Port HIVE-11544 to ...`, `TEZ-442 ... (part of TEZ-398)`, `HBASE-5715 Revert 'Instant schema alter' for now, HBASE-4213`) are therefore genuine.",
  "A key matched from a BRANCH NAME rather than prose is counted genuine. Two mechanisms occur: merge subjects (`Merge branch 'master' into KNOX-998-Package_Restructuring`) and svn trailers naming a branch (`.../branches/TEZ-1@1471779`). The association to the ticket is correct even though the commit does not implement it. The plan's five failure categories do not cover this case, so it is counted genuine and reported as a limitation rather than assigned an invented category.",
  "`revert` is used only where the SOLE matched key belongs to the reverted work and the commit has no ticket of its own -- i.e. a bare `Revert \"KEY-N: ...\"`. Where a project files a ticket to perform the revert (`KNOX-1755 - Revert upgrade httpclient ...`), that key is the commit's own work and is genuine."
 ],
